    'question_text' => 'A former client requests a copy of the treatment record. On the same day, opposing counsel in the client’s civil case serves the LCSW with a subpoena for the same record but provides no client authorization. The LCSW assumes both requests can be handled together.What is the LCSW’s most appropriate response?',
    'option_a' => 'Send the record to both requesters because the client’s access request waives privilege for the lawsuit',
