C. Correct. A lawful basis for restricting one portion of a record does not automatically justify withholding everything. The LCSW should provide access to the remaining information when reasonably possible. When HIPAA requires a written denial, the explanation should identify the reason for denial, whether independent review is available, how review may be requested, and how the client may file a complaint.

